You can set the execution context selector in Chrome DevTools via the console using several methods. Here are the most effective approaches:

## Method 1: Using `debug()` with a specific context

```javascript
// Set execution context to a specific iframe or window
debug(iframeElement.contentWindow);
```

## Method 2: Using `console.context()` (Chrome-specific)

```javascript
// Create a new console context for a specific frame
console.context(iframeElement.contentWindow);
```

## Method 3: Programmatically switching context

```javascript
// Get reference to the target window/frame
const targetWindow = document.getElementById('myIframe').contentWindow;

// Execute code in that context
targetWindow.eval('console.log("Running in iframe context")');
```

## Method 4: Using the Console API directly

```javascript
// Switch to a specific execution context
// This works when you have multiple frames/workers
const contexts = await chrome.devtools.inspectedWindow.getResources();
const targetContext = contexts.find(c => c.url.includes('target-page'));
```

